&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Sayari:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sayari is the judgment infrastructure for trustworthy AI in economic security and commercial risk. The Sayari Commercial World Model resolves 11.7B+ primary-source records from 250+ jurisdictions forming the ground truth of global commerce. A Judgment Ontology, encoding over a decade of investigative tradecraft, and Superconductor, an agentic orchestration platform, deliver AI that reasons like an expert analyst, shows its work, and traces every finding to its source. Trusted by U.S. Customs and Border Protection, HM Revenue &amp;amp; Customs, and Fortune 500 enterprises, Sayari is used by thousands of professionals across 35+ countries to secure supply chains and dismantle illicit networks. Headquartered in Washington, D.C., with offices in London, Singapore, Tokyo, and Tel Aviv.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION DESCRIPTION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a traditional sales engineering role. As a Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE), you are at the critical intersection of our code, our clients, and their most critical missions. You will be deployed to our most strategic partners, embedding within their environments to solve high-stakes problems that have no textbook answers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You own the &quot;last mile&quot; of our product&#39;s impact , ensuring our technology fundamentally transforms how our users confront challenges such as financial crime, supply chain disruption, and threats to national security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are equal parts engineer, strategist, and operator. One day you might be architecting a data pipeline within a client&#39;s cloud environment ; the next, you&#39;ll be writing production Python to integrate our API into a proprietary analytics platform ; and by the end of the week, you could be briefing a C-level executive, intelligence analyst, or mission director on the outcomes your work has enabled.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You thrive on ambiguity, operate with extreme ownership, and are relentless in your pursuit of delivering real-world value. You will act as a vital conduit between the front lines and our core engineering teams, turning your bespoke solutions into scalable, platform-wide features of Sayari’s product suite.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Sayari, we’re always looking for great talent to join our team. This is a proactive hiring post for future Forward Deployed Engineer roles, allowing us to connect with amazing candidates like you before a specific seat opens up.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOB RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embed and Build:&lt;/strong&gt; Deploy directly into our clients&#39; technical ecosystems and work with key stakeholders to understand their unique workflows, technical environments, and mission challenges. Design, build, and ship production-grade code. You will write robust Python applications, advanced SQL, and leverage our APIs to solve bespoke challenges at the edge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Outcome:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the entire technical lifecycle of our most strategic deployments, from initial discovery and architectural design to implementation and operationalization. You are responsible for ensuring our platform delivers tangible, mission-critical value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the Tip of the Spear:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary technical authority for our clients. You&#39;ll lead deep-dive technical workshops, debug complex systems, and act as a trusted, hands-on advisor on how to best leverage Sayari&#39;s platform to achieve their objectives in real-world investigations and missions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineer Solutions for the Mission:&lt;/strong&gt; Deconstruct ambiguous, high-level mission requirements into concrete technical solutions. Architect and implement scalable data models and workflows, ranging from building robust data pipelines into client persistence layers (Snowflake, Databricks, etc.) to developing custom Python scripts and prototyping AI/ML models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape Our Product:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the vital conduit between the front lines and our core engineering teams. You will translate complex, real-world operational needs and feedback into the next generation of Sayari&#39;s platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SKILLS &amp;amp; EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Required:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in a client-facing, technical role (Forward Deployed Engineer, Sales Engineering, Solutions Architecture, Technical Consulting, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to write clean, production-ready code, with strong proficiency in programming languages (preferably Python) and its data manipulation ecosystem (Pandas, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep fluency in writing and optimizing complex SQL queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on, practical experience consuming, integrating, and reasoning about RESTful APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to bridge the gap between code and mission. You can articulate highly technical concepts with clarity and conviction to engineers, analysts, and senior leaders alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills and the ability to navigate ambiguous, complex scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A relentless drive and intellectual curiosity. You are comfortable parachuting into new environments and learning new technologies on the fly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in a technical field strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience leveraging AI, including prompting Large Language Models (LLMs) or using their APIs to build analytical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and deploying solutions on cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, Azure) and familiarity with containerization (Docker, Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the modern data stack (e.g., Snowflake, Databricks) and workflow orchestrators (e.g., Airflow, Prefect).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of graph data technologies (Neo4j, TigerGraph) and their corresponding query languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to machine learning applications, particularly in NLP or entity resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in, or a demonstrated passion for, high-stakes domains such as AML/Financial Crime, Supply Chain Risk, or National Security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 50%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The target base salary for this position is £100,000 to £110,000 plus commission and equity. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors including location, local market variances, candidate experience and expertise, internal peer equity, and may vary from the amounts listed above.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% fully paid medical, vision, and dental for employees and their dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous time off; we observe all US federal holidays, close our office for a winter break (12/24-12/31), in addition to granting 18 PTO days and 10 sick days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding compensation package; competitive commissions for revenue roles and bonuses for non-revenue positions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligibility to participate in additional benefits such as 401k match up to 5%, 100% paid life insurance (up to $100,000 coverage),, and parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative and positive culture - your team will be as smart and driven as you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Limitless growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sayari is an equal opportunities employer. We are committed to building an inclusive workplace and a fair recruitment process. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds and do not discriminate on the basis of any protected characteristic under applicable UK law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£100,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£110,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h3&gt;Senior Medical Writer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;(Publications or Medical Affairs)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;London ,Manchester, Macclesfield, Glasgow, Hybrid or UK remote&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The power of three of the world&#39;s leading medical communications companies – Nucleus Global, ApotheCom and Ashfield MedComms – and the specialised services and skills within MEDiSTRAVA combine to form iNIZIO Medical. With over 2,000 employees globally, iNIZIO Medical creates compelling content and engage communities across the spectrum of healthcare. We improve scientific understanding and pioneer new ways of partnership, with a united vision to lead and define the future of medical in drug development and commercialisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to continuing growth within iNIZIO Medical we have some fantastic opportunities to join our teams across Nucleus Global, ApotheCom and Ashfield MedComms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Medical Writer with opportunities across multiple therapy areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role would suit an experienced Senior Medical Writer. It will provide a great career development opportunity for you with the support of a very experienced team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to a Scientific Director, you will develop scientific expertise in assigned therapeutic areas, supporting delivery for a versatile team. Core deliverable tasks include researching and developing technical materials, ensuring that a candidate or employee makes all outputs follow written brief, makes them accurate in content and editorial style, and references them. You will also communicate with clients and KOL on content development and attend scientific meetings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To succeed you will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Several years experience working within a medical communications agency environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· An academic background in the life sciences (Bachelor of Science, Master of Science, Doctor of Philosophy)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a great compensation package including pension, life insurance, private healthcare and paid time off. In addition to our benefits package, we are happy to talk flexible working with hybrid and remote working options available. We offer excellent opportunities for career and personal development, including opportunities to transfer your skills to our other agencies globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Pledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to promoting a culture of diversity, inclusion and belonging where everyone can bring each facet of themselves to work each day. We believe that strength in diversity and inclusivity is a driver of our success. We strive to accelerate the adoption and adherence of new medicines across the globe. We&#39;re determined to advance scientific understanding and pursue health equity for all. Inizio Medical is part of Inizio, a strategic partner for health and life sciences with a full suite of medical, marketing, advisory and engagement services.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.imgur.com/UuLTAa2.png&quot; alt=&quot;disability confident committed&quot; width=&quot;311&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

Fire, Health &amp; Safety Consultant - Contractor/Associate
Ark Workplace Risk | Competitive Day Rate&nbsp;
&nbsp;
At Ark Workplace Risk, we empower our clients to confidently manage risk, compliance, and safety through a trusted partnership built on expert knowledge, innovative solutions, and proactive guidance and insight.
&nbsp;
About Ark Workplace Risk:&nbsp;
Proven Expert Knowledge: With over 30 years of experience and a trusted reputation among 200+ UK organisations, we provide workable solutions that align with our clients' organisational and business goals, as well as regulatory requirements.
Industry-Leading Software: Our innovative tools streamline risk and compliance management, putting clients in control and enabling them to demonstrate accountability to stakeholders.
Insight-Driven Solutions: As industry thought leaders, we provide actionable insights into emerging legislation, guidance, and industry trends, ensuring court-readiness for their business.
Responsive Partnership: From every day, business-as-usual guidance to urgent, critical, complex, and contentious scenarios, we work in partnership with clients, becoming their trusted advisor and solution provider, whenever and wherever they need us most.
&nbsp;
Responsibilities:&nbsp;
&nbsp;

Undertake risk assessments including fire and health and safety, ensuring the fee earning target is met.&nbsp;
Undertake various fire, health and safety assignments within your competency.
Deliver client reports within the agreed SLA, in accordance with a forensic and pragmatic approach to ensure the Ark 'Gold Standard' is achieved.&nbsp;
Design health and safety site management systems where required, specific to client requirements.
Undertake onsite briefings and advise on risk management improvements.
Work collaboratively with a wide range of internal and external stakeholders.
Work with other consultants to ensure we are constantly sharing knowledge across the team.
Demonstrate a comprehensive understanding of controlling risks, compliances etc. in relation to our online management system QUOODA®

&nbsp;
The ideal candidate will have: 

At least 2+ years' fire, health &amp; safety risk assessment experience within the built environment in residential and/or commercial buildings
Good working knowledge of Approved Document B
Good working knowledge of BS 9999 / 9997
Education suitable to be competent to carry out Fire and Health &amp; Safety risk assessments on seven or more floors
The ability to undertake Fire Risk Assessments and General Risk Assessments at the same time
Articulate and clear communicators and report writing abilities as well as a comprehensive understanding of current UK regulations

&nbsp;
Qualifications

Must have NEBOSH General Certificate in Health &amp; Safety or equivalent as minimum.
Must have a minimum of a level 3 in fire safety/fire risk
Recognised fire safety memberships e.g. AIFireE, MIFireE, GIFireE, MIFSM etc.
Willing to apply for or have registered on any of the following fire risk assessors registers IFSM, FRACS, IFPO or IFE

&nbsp;
Practical Requirements:&nbsp;
Ability to facilitate hybrid working with home office that is suitable for connectivity to the office and clients, a safe and productive place to work conducive for delivering daily duties.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

